<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<style>
  body { font-family: Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif; max-width: 640px; margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 22px; color: #222; line-height: 1.6; }
  h1 { font-size: 1.4rem; margin: 0 0 .3em; }
  .sub { color: #777; margin: 0 0 1.4em; }
  ol { padding-left: 1.3em; }
  li { margin: .35em 0; }
  .box { background: #f4f4f4; border: 1px solid #ddd; border-radius: 6px; padding: 14px 16px; }
  a { color: #b5341f; }
  .cap { color: #888; font-size: .82rem; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
  <h1>Monday heads-up &mdash; what's popular this week</h1>
  <p class="sub">Source: {{ source | default('Letterboxd, popular this week') }}. A preview of
    what Wednesday night's digest will likely carry, so you can watch a couple before Thursday
    and write from real viewing.
    {% if source_note %}<br><em>{{ source_note }}</em>{% endif %}</p>

  <ol>
    {% for f in films %}
    <li><a href="{{ f.url }}">{{ f.title }}</a>{% if f.year %} ({{ f.year }}){% endif %}</li>
    {% endfor %}
  </ol>

  <div class="box">
    <strong>When Thursday's draft lands:</strong> reply with a film and your take to swap it
    into the roundup, for example &ldquo;feature Obsession instead, I watched it Tuesday &mdash;
    here's what I thought: ...&rdquo;. One reply with your notes, then <strong>approve</strong>.
    <br><br>
    The long horror deep-dive film is chosen Thursday from the actual digest, so it is not
    locked yet. If Thursday's pick is not the one you want, say so in your reply and put some
    substance behind it.
    <br><br>
    <strong>Last week's issue:</strong> if you have not posted the social copy yet, this is
    your nudge to do it.
  </div>

  <p class="cap">Ranks shift a little between now and Wednesday, and the odd title drops in or
    out, but the top of the list is usually stable by today.</p>
</body>
</html>
